{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_decisions_0010_agent_edits_immediate_agent_edits", "label": "D-10: agent edits applied immediately, highlighted, rolled back via version history", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/decisions/0010-agent-edits.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "\u0420\u0415\u0428\u0415\u041d\u041e (2026-10-25). Chosen over suggestions-for-approval: fast, the agent works autonomously without waiting for a human; the cost is the need for a good version history. Handwriting anchors survive because they are CRDT relative positions. Refined by D-45 for notes created wholly by an agent."}, {"id": "docs_decisions_0010_agent_edits_suggestions_for_approval", "label": "Rejected option: agent suggestions awaiting user approval", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/decisions/0010-agent-edits.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Full control, but friction: the agent 'waits' for the human."}, {"id": "docs_decisions_0010_agent_edits_version_history", "label": "Version history as rollback mechanism for agent edits", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/decisions/0010-agent-edits.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_decisions_0010_agent_edits_crdt_relative_anchors", "label": "Handwriting anchors as CRDT relative positions (not broken by agent edits)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/decisions/0010-agent-edits.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_decisions_0010_agent_edits_immediate_agent_edits", "target": "docs_decisions_0010_agent_edits_suggestions_for_approval", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/decisions/0